        ],
        "paragraph": "The ARTELEA free standing luminaire represents the first product by the Zumtobel brand to include a return for remanufacturing option at the end of a light-as-a-service (LaaS) contract to permit an additional usage phase. The remanufacturing process includes the following:\n- $\\rightarrow$ Disassembly of the luminaire\n- $\\rightarrow$ Disassembly of the luminaire\n- $\\rightarrow$ Cleaning of the components\n- $\\rightarrow$ Replacement of used components\n- $\\rightarrow$ A function and safety test\nPlans call for the availability of an active remanufacturing option for 10% of the Zumtobel Group's product families by 2030.\nThe circular systems concept used for ARTELEA addresses the following usage cycles in agreement with the Zumtobel Group's circular economy strategy:\n- $\\rightarrow$ Maintenance & upgrade/refurbishment kits Longest possible product service life for the customer through the availability of replacement and upgrade components\n- $\\rightarrow$ Maintenance & upgrade/refurbishment kits Longest possible product service life for the customer through the availability of replacement and upgrade components\n- $\\rightarrow$ Remanufacturing Return and remanufacturing service a spart of an LaaS contract\n- $\\rightarrow$ Controlled return to the WEEE recycling system Return and controlled WEEE recycling within the framework of the LaaS contract when the product is no longer suitable for reprocessing",
