        "paragraph": "A central aspect of wastewater disposal is the complete canalisation of the sealed areas situated airside. Rainwater run-off is led from the individual drainage areas of the airport - runways, aprons and taxiways alone make up an area of more than 2.5 million square metres  $-$  to the central wastewater disposal plant. The pollution level of the wastewater is measured on line where the main collector enters the central wastewater disposal plant.\nAs a result of the targeted separation of polluted from non-polluted wastewater, it has been possible to reduce the volume of wastewater to be processed in the treatment plant. FWAG's wastewater (Vienna site) amounted to 350.573 m<sup>3</sup> in 2023.",
