          "**Hybrid working model**"
        ],
        "subtitles": [],
        "paragraph": "During the Covid-19 pandemic, we discovered that working from home can be very productive. At the same time, however, working from home can also result in a lack of social and personal interaction and mutual learning. For this reason, we have decided to adopt a hybrid working model, which combines personal interaction and excellent office equipment with the flexibility of working remotely. Following a pilot phase, we entered into a works agreement on mobile working in the summer of 2023, on the basis of which employees work in the office on at least two days per week. We pursue an approach based on trust and communication: teams organise themselves and decide which days they come to the office. In addition, employees may work from abroad for a certain period of time if business requirements as well as legal and tax risks permit, conditions that are examined in an approval process.",
        "classification": "ESG",
        "report_name": "Scout24_SE.pdf"
