          "Defined contribution pension system"
        ],
        "paragraph": "The rules of the defined contribution pension scheme apply to Theodor Weimer, Christoph Böhm, Heike Eckert, Stephan Leithner and Gregor Pottmeyer.\nUnder the defined contribution pension scheme, the company makes an annual capital contribution to the scheme for each calendar year that a member serves on the Executive Board. This pension contribution is calculated by applying an individual contribution rate to their pensionable income. The Supervisory Board determines and regularly reviews the pensionable income. The annual capital contributions calculated in this way bear interest of at least 3 per cent per annum. As a rule, retirement benefits are paid as a monthly pension. However, the Executive Board member may choose for payment to be made in the form of a one-off lump sum or as five instalments. The entitlements vest in accordance with the provisions of Betriebsrentengesetz (German Company Pensions Act).",
        "classification": "ESG",
        "report_name": "Deutsche_Börse_AG.pdf"
