        "paragraph": "For the financial year 2023, ANDRITZ reported a total turnover of 8,660.0 MEUR. Of this, 2,931.5 MEUR, or 33.9%, was categorized as Taxonomy-eligible. This eligible turnover is split into two main categories: Taxonomy-aligned activities (A.1) and Taxonomy-eligible but not environmentally sustainable activities (A.2). Taxonomy-aligned activities (A.1) amounted to 2,055.7 MEUR, representing 23.7% of the total turnover. All of this aligned turnover (100% based on 'Of which Enabling') was classified as 'Enabling' activity. Within A.1, two specific economic activities were identified: 1. CCM 3.1. Manufacture of renewable energy technologies: This activity generated 2,020.5 MEUR, accounting for 23.3% of total turnover. It substantially contributed to Climate Change Mitigation ('Y') and was not applicable for assessment (N/EL) for Climate Change Adaptation, Water, Pollution, Circular Economy, or Biodiversity. Critically, this activity met all 'Do No Significant Harm' (DNSH) criteria, confirming 'Y' for Climate Change Mitigation, Climate Change Adaptation, Water, Pollution, Circular Economy, Biodiversity, and Minimum Safeguards. In 2022, its proportion of Taxonomy aligned turnover was 23.2%. This activity is classified as 'Enabling'. 2. CCM 3.20. Manufacture, installation, and servicing of high, medium and low voltage electrical equipment for electrical transmission and distribution that result in or enable a substantial contribution to climate change mitigation: This activity contributed 35.2 MEUR, or 0.4% of total turnover. It substantially contributed to Climate Change Mitigation ('Y') and was not applicable for assessment (N/EL) for Climate Change Adaptation, Water, Pollution, Circular Economy, or Biodiversity. Similar to CCM 3.1, it met all DNSH criteria, confirming 'Y' for Climate Change Mitigation, Climate Change Adaptation, Water, Pollution, Circular Economy, Biodiversity, and Minimum Safeguards. Its proportion of Taxonomy aligned turnover in 2022 was not applicable ('N/A'). This activity is also classified as 'Enabling'. Taxonomy-eligible but not environmentally sustainable activities (A.2) totaled 875.8 MEUR, comprising 10.1% of the total turnover. For this category, 41% of the turnover was eligible for substantial contribution criteria, while 59% did not meet DNSH criteria or minimum safeguards. Two specific activities were identified here: 1. CCM 3.6. Manufacture of other low carbon technologies: This activity accounted for 361.0 MEUR, 4.2% of total turnover. It was eligible ('EL') for substantial contribution to Climate Change Mitigation, but not eligible ('N/EL') for Climate Change Adaptation, Water, Pollution, Circular Economy, or Biodiversity. Furthermore, it was not eligible ('N/EL') for any of the seven DNSH criteria, including Climate Change Mitigation, Climate Change Adaptation, Water, Pollution, Circular Economy, Biodiversity, and Minimum Safeguards. Its proportion of eligible turnover in 2022 was 4.7%. 2. CE 5.1. Repair, refurbishment and remanufacturing: This activity generated 514.8 MEUR, or 5.9% of total turnover. It was eligible ('EL') for substantial contribution to Circular Economy, but not eligible ('N/EL') for Climate Change Mitigation, Climate Change Adaptation, Water, Pollution, or Biodiversity. Regarding DNSH, it was eligible ('EL') for the Circular Economy criterion but not eligible ('N/EL') for Climate Change Mitigation, Climate Change Adaptation, Water, Pollution, Biodiversity, or Minimum Safeguards. Its proportion of eligible turnover in 2022 was not applicable ('N/A'). Overall, 82% of the total taxonomy-eligible turnover was identified as having a substantial contribution, while 18% did not meet all DNSH criteria or minimum safeguards. The proportion of total taxonomy-eligible turnover in 2022 was 27.9%. Finally, Taxonomy-non-eligible activities constituted the largest portion of turnover, amounting to 5,728.5 MEUR, or 66.1% of the total turnover.",
